<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/1st-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Alamance</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">16 May 1771</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Alamance was fought on 16 May 1771 in North Carolina, where Governor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-tryon">William Tryon</a>'s militia defeated about 2,000 Regulators, backcountry farmers protesting against corrupt officials and excessive fees. The Regulators were poorly armed and led, and several were later hanged for treason. The battle ended the Regulator movement.</p></div>
